VALUES (
  'rmsnorm',
  'Implement RMSNorm',
  'Medium',
  '基础层',
  'rms_norm',
  '# 🟡 Medium: Implement RMSNorm

Implement **Root Mean Square Layer Normalization** — the normalization used in LLaMA, Gemma, etc.

$$\text{RMSNorm}(x) = \frac{x}{\text{RMS}(x)} \cdot w, \quad \text{RMS}(x) = \sqrt{\frac{1}{d}\sum x_i^2 + \epsilon}$$

### Signature
```python
def rms_norm(x: torch.Tensor, weight: torch.Tensor, eps: float = 1e-6) -> torch.Tensor:
    # Normalize over the last dimension. No mean subtraction (unlike LayerNorm).
```

### Rules
- Do **NOT** use any built-in norm layers
- Normalize over `dim=-1`
- Must support autograd',
  'def rms_norm(x: torch.Tensor, weight: torch.Tensor, eps: float = 1e-6) -> torch.Tensor:',
  '',
  'RMS(x) = sqrt(mean(x^2) + eps). RMSNorm(x) = x / RMS(x) * weight. Simpler than LayerNorm — no mean subtraction.',
  '# ✏️ YOUR IMPLEMENTATION HERE

def rms_norm(x, weight, eps=1e-6):
    pass  # Replace this',
  '[{"name": "Basic behavior", "code": "\nimport torch\nx = torch.randn(2, 8)\nweight = torch.ones(8)\nout = {fn}(x, weight)\nassert out.shape == x.shape, f''Shape mismatch: {out.shape}''\nrms = torch.sqrt(x.pow(2).mean(dim=-1, keepdim=True) + 1e-6)\nref = x / rms * weight\nassert torch.allclose(out, ref, atol=1e-5), ''Value mismatch''\n"}, {"name": "With learned weight", "code": "\nimport torch\nx = torch.randn(4, 16)\nweight = torch.randn(16)\nout = {fn}(x, weight)\nrms = torch.sqrt(x.pow(2).mean(dim=-1, keepdim=True) + 1e-6)\nref = x / rms * weight\nassert torch.allclose(out, ref, atol=1e-5), ''Value mismatch with non-trivial weight''\n"}, {"name": "3-D input", "code": "\nimport torch\nx = torch.randn(2, 4, 32)\nweight = torch.ones(32)\nout = {fn}(x, weight)\nassert out.shape == x.shape, f''Shape mismatch on 3-D: {out.shape}''\nrms = torch.sqrt(x.pow(2).mean(dim=-1, keepdim=True) + 1e-6)\nref = x / rms * weight\nassert torch.allclose(out, ref, atol=1e-5), ''Value mismatch on 3-D''\n"}, {"name": "Gradient flow", "code": "\nimport torch\nx = torch.randn(2, 8, requires_grad=True)\nweight = torch.ones(8, requires_grad=True)\nout = {fn}(x, weight)\nout.sum().backward()\nassert x.grad is not None, ''x.grad is None''\nassert weight.grad is not None, ''weight.grad is None''\n"}]',
  '# ✅ SOLUTION

def rms_norm(x, weight, eps=1e-6):
    rms = torch.sqrt(x.pow(2).mean(dim=-1, keepdim=True) + eps)
    return x / rms * weight',
  '# 🟡 Solution: Implement RMSNorm

Reference solution for Root Mean Square Normalization.',
  'approved',
  6
)
