INSERT INTO problems (slug, title, difficulty, category, function_name, description, signature, example, hint, template_code, tests_json, solution_code, solution_markdown, status, sort_order)
VALUES (
  'linear_attention',
  'Linear Self-Attention',
  'Hard',
  '注意力机制',
  'linear_attention',
  '# 🔴 Hard: Linear Self-Attention

Implement **Linear Attention** — O(S·D²) instead of O(S²·D), enabling efficient long-sequence processing.

Replace softmax with a **kernel feature map** $\phi$:

$$\text{LinearAttn}(Q,K,V) = \frac{\phi(Q) \left(\phi(K)^T V\right)}{\phi(Q) \cdot \sum \phi(K)}$$

### Feature map
Use $\phi(x) = \text{elu}(x) + 1$ (ensures non-negative features).

### Signature
```python
def linear_attention(Q, K, V):
    # Q: (B, S, D_k), K: (B, S, D_k), V: (B, S, D_v)
    # Returns: (B, S, D_v)
```

### Key insight
Instead of computing the $S \times S$ attention matrix, compute $\phi(K)^T V$ first (a $D_k \times D_v$ matrix), then multiply by $\phi(Q)$.

### Rules
- Must use a feature map (NOT softmax)
- Must be O(S·D²) — should run fast on long sequences
- You **may** use `F.elu`',
  'def linear_attention(Q, K, V):',
  '',
  'Feature map: phi(x) = elu(x) + 1. Compute phi(Q) @ (phi(K)^T @ V) instead of softmax(Q @ K^T) @ V. Normalize by phi(Q) @ sum(phi(K)).',
  '# ✏️ YOUR IMPLEMENTATION HERE

def linear_attention(Q, K, V):
    pass  # Replace this',
  '[{"name": "Output shape", "code": "\nimport torch\nout = {fn}(torch.randn(2, 8, 16), torch.randn(2, 8, 16), torch.randn(2, 8, 32))\nassert out.shape == (2, 8, 32), f''Shape mismatch: {out.shape}''\n"}, {"name": "No NaN or Inf", "code": "\nimport torch\ntorch.manual_seed(0)\nout = {fn}(torch.randn(2, 16, 8), torch.randn(2, 16, 8), torch.randn(2, 16, 8))\nassert not torch.isnan(out).any(), ''NaN in output''\nassert not torch.isinf(out).any(), ''Inf in output''\n"}, {"name": "Gradient flow", "code": "\nimport torch\nQ = torch.randn(1, 4, 8, requires_grad=True)\nK = torch.randn(1, 4, 8, requires_grad=True)\nV = torch.randn(1, 4, 8, requires_grad=True)\n{fn}(Q, K, V).sum().backward()\nassert Q.grad is not None and K.grad is not None and V.grad is not None, ''Missing gradients''\n"}, {"name": "Runs fast on long sequences (linear complexity)", "code": "\nimport torch, time\ntorch.manual_seed(0)\nQ = torch.randn(1, 2048, 64)\nK = torch.randn(1, 2048, 64)\nV = torch.randn(1, 2048, 64)\nt0 = time.perf_counter()\nfor _ in range(10):\n    {fn}(Q, K, V)\nelapsed = time.perf_counter() - t0\nassert elapsed < 5.0, f''Too slow: {elapsed:.2f}s — should be O(S*D^2) not O(S^2*D)''\n"}]',
  '# ✅ SOLUTION

def linear_attention(Q, K, V):
    Q_prime = F.elu(Q) + 1
    K_prime = F.elu(K) + 1
    KV = torch.bmm(K_prime.transpose(1, 2), V)       # (B, D_k, D_v)
    Z = K_prime.sum(dim=1, keepdim=True)              # (B, 1, D_k)
    num = torch.bmm(Q_prime, KV)                      # (B, S, D_v)
    den = torch.bmm(Q_prime, Z.transpose(1, 2))       # (B, S, 1)
    return num / (den + 1e-6)',
  '# 🔴 Solution: Linear Self-Attention

Reference solution — kernel-based attention with elu+1 feature map.',
  'approved',
  10
)
